407
00:29:54,926 --> 00:30:03,236
That said, I found myself often in the same scenario where I would see a PR complete from a thread in any agentic tool.

408
00:30:03,408 --> 00:30:09,828
I would go over, I would see a bunch of comments, and I would copy paste the ones I agreed with back to the thread and say, fix these.

409
00:30:10,094 --> 00:30:13,968
This was really inefficient and obnoxious, so I made a skill to do it for me instead.

410
00:30:14,318 --> 00:30:16,448
The babysit skill is actually quite simple.

411
00:30:16,622 --> 00:30:21,892
It tells the agent, hey, this PR probably has comments from automated reviewers.

412
00:30:22,286 --> 00:30:23,428
I want you to keep an eye on it.

413
00:30:23,790 --> 00:30:28,132
Take a look every time automated review comments come in and decide if they're worth addressing.

414
00:30:28,398 --> 00:30:34,788
If they are, make the changes, push them, and keep monitoring the PR to see if the agents resolve their comments.

415
00:30:35,168 --> 00:30:43,716
This one little skill is a super simple, maybe one and a half paragraph pile of text that creates a loop.

416
00:30:43,968 --> 00:30:47,728
The loop is the agent makes the changes, files the PR.

417
00:30:47,888 --> 00:30:50,596
We have all of our automated review bots giving feedback.

418
00:30:50,862 --> 00:30:57,668
And this agent will now autonomously address the feedback and keep improving the PR until none of those review bots have anything else to say.

419
00:30:57,934 --> 00:31:01,568
At which point it will finally go from working to done.

420
00:31:01,870 --> 00:31:06,404
